I am testing `conformance.kernel.recovery`. The `recover_json_object` function is designed to prefer the last top-level object in the text if no code fences are present. If I provide a reply containing two separate JSON objects, the kernel should recover the second one. If I rewrite the input to merge these into a single object (by wrapping them in a list or a parent object), the recovered value changes from the second object to the combined structure. This confirms that the recovery kernel's 'last-wins' logic for top-level objects is functioning as described in the docstring.